Workspace (@workspace: 0) {
The best workspace should blur the barrier between programs, making them feel like parts of a whole. With many features in a base app, we can make each appearance of a workflow enjoy the level of control of a CAD in a molecule scale, the reality of a street-view with a fake castle mashed together, or the plentiful level of metadata that exists around one specific idea, it's automations, transfers, definitions...

Such workspace would have the possibility of opening apps in windows normally, being a wayland compositor or something better, and being able to spawn Lince's native components/widgets: Sands, Castles, Areas of Influence... So it has available to the experience Lince gives to the user the usage of all the programs in the world the user wants. The extra work is baking it into a generic program in a way that elevates each experience, being an improvement over the original idea if possible and an ever growing combination of ways one can combine the growing features together.

The applications of such generic interface space should be able to bring about from UI/UX editing and prototyping to molecular editing, protein folding environments and hardware engineering, from circuits to GPUs, with full behavior correctness of the tecnical aspects. The more these capabilities are tiny abstractions over robust and generic native primitives the better.

The wording of workspace can be broken down if you want to philosophise, workspace, work space. If i can have a generic digital experience, easy to mold to fit my Needs, we should also be able to have a fluent integration with hardware that can do the same. Moving closer to science-fiction in the time of writing this, but with a good enough plan, it's not fiction, just a lot of work.

What would be the capabilities of a work space? How can hardware be generic? By definition it is hard ware. Doing this would be a revolution in tecnology, having the things we use hardware today for be completely dynamic. Those that have studied the common sense of academia or played so far with hardware have dust in their eyes by current experience. History can find you many instances of the flipping of the board happening under completely contrary common sense. Can you at least give it one second of plausibility? Or are you under the spell?

The hipotetical dynamicware would be a blob of something undistinguishable from biology or technology. An Ailuros is the melting of barriers between software and hardware inside the cocoon, to emerge into something better. Such dynamicware would have shape and materials as the defining programmed capabilities in the micro of what we deem like software programs and macro of what we think of components to a computer like cameras and microprocessors.

This dynamicware could easily be turned into your laboratory of exploration. It should be self composable, easy to change, conserve and preserve. It should be able to help you on your day to day with what you need, follow you around, energize itself, and not get in your way.

The immediate form of this is proving it can be done in prototype form, with a non-prototype and fully functioning workspace, that can model anything, the scale, concept, relationships, behavior, is but a configuration.

Modeling things in Lince is also a Need. So if i have a Need to model something as big as the observable universe or bigger i should be able to, computers handle scale well, an i128 is enough. Setting a boundary on a part of the universe gives us a sandbox, if we have an Earth globe at our disposal to create these areas we may edit them to escape to fantasy land. I take the place that is my house on the map and put all my Needs and Contributions, relay it as being from my city for privacy. I look at things that are Needed in the areas close to me, or in the other side of the planet, I make transfers with them, of physical resources, information, services...

I automate workflows, and I create scenarios on top of visualizations of the real world. I take tools like Gaussian Splatting, photos, videos to see what the world is like in the present, and I overlap it, mesh it together with my assets, the structures I create, using tools like game engines, blender, CAD, Generative World Models to transform the digital representation of the world, taking the real version or the simulated, gamified one and create the Needs and model the Contributions related to it, assign Actors to take care of them. Possibly doing that without interacting with Lince. That's the goal.

For that a system that allows for maximum control of the scenes, is needed, the freedom of Minecraft with real world data and tiny, tiny voxels or something better. That would be the end of the Lince's interface, nothing grater is justified to be built according to the philosophy. It would easily be able to display current web pages, launch other systems and games inside it. You open Lince, it has everything you should Need, and give you freedom to do anything you want in it's digital representation, connected completely with the real world if you want it.

- [ ] Physics' "periodic table"
- [ ] Proteins and cellular automata.
- [ ] CAD with different materials, drinking from previous smaller scale fields. Modeling mechanical structures and electrical parts (from circuit to GPUs and beyond). Lince should support native parametric CAD for reusable, connectable parts, with dimensions, tolerances and build instructions linked to Records.
- [ ] With the interface that has virtually limitless scale, we focus on centering the experience on the user's interest, Earth's globe as a 3D space with it's real topography, updateable in real time. The earth is default data, not a hardcoded place we need to make the user spend time on.
- [ ] In any scale, one can take what is there as a point in which the components/widgets/sands/visual tools have at their disposal will be in a size it is good to work with, either locking things to the HUD with pinned sands, or putting them geographically in one region of the space: only in their house when they zoom in the map into their room, or the part of the room in space that is their desk, and inside they will see their widgets. In summary going from 3D to 2D, where you feel more productive with the dimensions you want.
- [ ] Analyzing with Fiote what some part of the space we are seeing is, and the possible Needs/Contributions we care about.
- [ ] View the future simulation of such world based on the possible Automations and Transfers that will happen, as transformations and scenarios of the Space, versions of it, mixed in a same scene, like if 50% transparency, some house that can be built, as if i'm planning a farm in a property and i'm putting down in the simulation where each resource will be, and after setting them, taking the unfinished work, exploding it into each tiny part and Assigning it to contrActors in Lince and doing it myself too.
- [ ] Character modeling, edit mode with high realism and normal mode focusing on joints. Spore-like.

That and more is the scope of the Workspace work before we start dealing with Hardware in Ailuros, all of the crazy ideas of Dynamicware are not to be thought of in the plan of Workspace, they are some natural conclusion to Lince meeting Needs, with the least amount of moving parts, for now it should be focused on software of the tasks above. Later features of robotics will redefine the capabilities of the workspace, having even more integration with reality with projectors and cameras to sync actions in the real world with actions in Lince. For now we whould focus on having the best software experience we can with our Workspace integrating everything the user uses in a computer.

Development is organized in [Workspace development](interface/workspace/Workspace-Development.lingua), with verified shared foundations, explicit feature dependencies and parallel branches where their interfaces permit it.

